  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25616754",
      "title": "Analyzing the Created Project",
      "sourceHash": "e6d04798335ea51f944548d7763d680eed3e1646e3cce475d1696203b114a53a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.46,
          "end": 5.29,
          "en": "So we did create that NextJS project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.29,
          "end": 9.27,
          "en": "here in the terminal with NPX create-next-app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.27,
          "end": 11.87,
          "en": "and that gave us a folder which looks like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.87,
          "end": 14.03,
          "en": "which has this kind of content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.03,
          "end": 17.3,
          "en": "Attached, you also find that starting project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.3,
          "end": 21.16,
          "en": "in case it changes over time or looks slightly different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.16,
          "end": 24.73,
          "en": "because the starting template was changed, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.73,
          "end": 28.2,
          "en": "So attached, you find that exact project snapshot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.2,
          "end": 29.75,
          "en": "which I have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.75,
          "end": 32.69,
          "en": "If you do download the attached snapshot though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.69,
          "end": 36,
          "en": "there is one extra step you need to go through.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36,
          "end": 38.04,
          "en": "You need to open the terminal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.04,
          "end": 40.95,
          "en": "and you can use the one built into Visual Studio Code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.95,
          "end": 43.04,
          "en": "which is your default terminal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.04,
          "end": 44.77,
          "en": "Your default command prompt",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.77,
          "end": 47.21,
          "en": "which ships with your operating system,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.21,
          "end": 50.98,
          "en": "just already integrated into Visual Studio Code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.98,
          "end": 54.45,
          "en": "and conveniently, also already navigated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.45,
          "end": 56.36,
          "en": "into this project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.36,
          "end": 58.11,
          "en": "So any commands you run here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.11,
          "end": 61.71,
          "en": "will execute in the context of your project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.71,
          "end": 64.54,
          "en": "And here you then need to run npm install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.54,
          "end": 67.53,
          "en": "if you use that attached snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.53,
          "end": 68.81,
          "en": "Because that will then install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.81,
          "end": 70.86,
          "en": "all the dependencies of this project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.86,
          "end": 73.15,
          "en": "as defined here in package.json,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.15,
          "end": 76.3,
          "en": "and store them and their dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.3,
          "end": 78.6,
          "en": "in the node modules folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.6,
          "end": 81.7,
          "en": "So that's also a folder in which will never work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.7,
          "end": 84.49,
          "en": "The three important folders for us here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.49,
          "end": 87.03,
          "en": "are pages, public, and styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.03,
          "end": 91.15,
          "en": "though pages is by far the most important one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.15,
          "end": 94.37,
          "en": "Styles, as you might guess, holds some style files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.37,
          "end": 95.88,
          "en": "We can ignore that for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 95.88,
          "end": 97.46000000000001,
          "en": "We'll work on that soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 97.46000000000001,
          "end": 102.46000000000001,
          "en": "And public simply holds public resources our page might use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.75999999999999,
          "end": 105.41,
          "en": "Something like images, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 105.41,
          "end": 108.11,
          "en": "Now one thing you might see here in public though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 108.11,
          "end": 111.7,
          "en": "is that unlike in a regular React app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.7,
          "end": 113.03999999999999,
          "en": "which you, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 113.03999999999999,
          "end": 116.82,
          "en": "created with create React app with that extra tool,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.82,
          "end": 119.63,
          "en": "that there in a standard React app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 119.63,
          "end": 123.12,
          "en": "you have a index HTML file in the public folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.12,
          "end": 126.78,
          "en": "Here in the NextJS app, you don't have that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.78,
          "end": 127.96,
          "en": "And the reason for this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.96,
          "end": 131.4,
          "en": "is that NextJS has this built in pre-rendering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.4,
          "end": 134.38,
          "en": "And whilst it gives you a single page application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 134.38,
          "end": 137.79,
          "en": "that single page is dynamically pre-rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 137.79,
          "end": 140.74,
          "en": "when a request reaches the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 140.74,
          "end": 145.74,
          "en": "so that you do return an initial page with content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 146.21,
          "end": 149.86,
          "en": "That is what I talked about earlier in this course as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 149.86,
          "end": 154.06,
          "en": "This server-side rendering and the pre-rendering of pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.06,
          "end": 154.893,
          "en": "And hence for us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 154.893,
          "end": 158.21,
          "en": "the pages folder will be the most important folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 158.21,
          "end": 160.48,
          "en": "because that is where we will set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.48,
          "end": 162.32,
          "en": "that file based routing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 162.32,
          "end": 164.07,
          "en": "and that is there for the folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 164.07,
          "end": 167.68,
          "en": "which is important for us to define the different pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 167.68,
          "end": 170.563,
          "en": "that should make up our application here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}